1. `web/src/notorganic-provider/index.ts:58-69` — severity 3, confidence 0.99

```ts
	const response = await fetcher(`/api/notorganic/provider/${path}`, init);
	const body = await response.json().catch(() => ({}));
	if (!response.ok) {
		const message =
			typeof body?.error?.message === "string"
				? body.error.message
				: typeof body?.message === "string"
					? body.message
					: `Not Organic request failed (${response.status})`;
		throw new Error(message);
	}
	return body as T;
```

JSON parsing failures are discarded. A 2xx response with an empty, malformed, or non-JSON body becomes a successful `{}` result. Account/wallet callers can consequently report a connected session and display `undefined · Wallet connected` instead of surfacing the provider contract failure.

