`providerJson<T>` casts arbitrary network data—or the empty-object parse fallback—to any requested result type without validation. Consequently, functions declared to return `NotOrganicAccount`, `NotOrganicWallet`, or `NotOrganicUsage` can resolve with structurally invalid values while callers compile under false guarantees. The response should be parsed as `unknown` and validated per endpoint before returning.

